# Interview Talking Points

**Question**

> Why did you use Heap Percentage for the Gauge but Heap Bytes for the historical graph?

**Example Response**

> The Gauge is intended to communicate operational health quickly, so percentages are easier to interpret. The Time Series graph is intended for deeper analysis. Displaying heap usage in bytes makes Garbage Collection patterns and memory growth much easier to observe. Using both representations provides immediate visibility while preserving detailed diagnostic information.

---

# Lessons Learned During Implementation

One of the most valuable design decisions during implementation was separating operational monitoring from diagnostic monitoring.

Current health is best represented using percentages.

Historical analysis is better represented using raw values.

Using the appropriate visualization for each purpose significantly improves dashboard usability.

